cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use DOMINOANN in your research, please cite it using these metadata."

title: "DOMINOANN v1.0: Data Ontology Mapping Integration for Non-model Organism Annotation"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Umashankar"
    given-names: "Vetrivel"
    affiliation: "Indian Council of Medical Research - National Institute for Research in Tuberculosis (ICMR-NIRT), Chennai, India"

  - family-names: "Jayaraman"
    given-names: "Roja"
    affiliation: "Indian Council of Medical Research - National Institute for Research in Tuberculosis (ICMR-NIRT), Chennai, India"

  - family-names: "Eden"
    given-names: "Infanta Saleth Teresa M"
    affiliation: "Indian Council of Medical Research - National Institute for Research in Tuberculosis (ICMR-NIRT), Chennai, India"

version: "1.0"

abstract: >
  DOMINOANN v1.0 is a fully automated Bash- and R-based workflow with a
  Zenity graphical user interface for functional enrichment analysis of
  non-model organisms using differentially expressed genes. The pipeline
  automatically retrieves organism-specific annotation resources, constructs
  customized annotation databases, and performs Gene Ontology and KEGG
  pathway enrichment analysis with integrated visualization.

keywords:
  - non-model organisms
  - functional annotation
  - gene ontology
  - KEGG
  - enrichment analysis
  - differential gene expression
  - bioinformatics
  - computational biology
  - Bash
  - R
  - Zenity
  - annotation database

license: "GPL-3.0"

repository-code: "https://github.com/inpacdb/DOMINOANN"

url: "https://github.com/inpacdb/DOMINOANN"
